  (text "4-wire SPI mode strap: IM0=GND, IM1=+3V3, IM2=+3V3 (pins 36/37/38)" (at 227.38 192.63 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top))
    (uuid fd579777-85c2-47f6-9424-51d3b0359641)
  )
  (text "Display subsystem (pilink-7el.5) -- Crystalfontz CFAF240320A0-024SN, 240x320 native\n(rotated 90deg to 320x240 in firmware via ST7789V MADCTL/MV), 4-wire SPI.\nJ501 pin table sourced directly from Crystalfontz's own datasheet (Rev 1v2, 2021-03-26),\nsection 6, SPI-mode column (4-wire SPI selected via IM0=0/IM1=1/IM2=1). SDO (pin 4) and\nTE (pin 5) are marked no-connect per the datasheet (write-only use, no tearing-effect\nsync needed). DB0-17 (pins 6-23), DOTCLK (26), ENABLE (28), VSYNC (29), HSYNC (30) and\nRD (31) are all tied to GND per the datasheet's explicit 'fix low if not used' guidance\nfor the unused parallel-bus/RGB-interface pins -- not left floating. IM0 (36) is also\ntied GND and IM1/IM2 (37/38) to +3V3 for the 4-wire SPI mode strap. VCC (3) and VCI (39)\nboth go to +3V3 (digital I/O and analog display power rails, both 3.3V per the\ndatasheet). This sheet's own +3V3/GND power symbols don't drive those nets --\npower.kicad_sch does -- same convention as every other populated child sheet in this\nproject (see their own notes for why a per-sheet power_pin_not_driven ERC result on\nstandalone single-sheet checks is expected and not a real defect)." (at 20 300 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid b643acd0-f8ee-43e6-be49-3f6c609cbf5d)
  )
  (text "Connector: J501 is the LCSC AFC01-S40FCA-00 (C262674, Jushuo), 40-position, 0.5mm\npitch, bottom-contact, flip-top-lock SMT FPC/ZIF connector -- confirmed directly from\nits own LCSC spec table (pitch/position-count/contact-style/locking-feature all match\nthe panel's own '40 Position, 0.50mm Pitch ZIF connector' spec and its 500mA/50V rating\nis comfortably above this interface's actual currents). No stock KiCad symbol or\nfootprint exists for this exact part, so both were hand-authored for this bead\n(pico_link_custom:CFAF240320A0_FPC40 in symbols/pico_link_custom.kicad_sym;\nConnector_FPC:AFC01-S40FCA-00 in footprints/Connector_FPC.pretty/, registered in\nfp-lib-table). The symbol's single-column pin layout is a schematic drawing\nconvenience, not a physical pinout diagram -- pin *numbers* match the datasheet\nexactly, which is what the netlist cares about. The footprint's pad pitch/position\ncount/bottom-contact style are confirmed against the part's own LCSC spec table, but\nthe exact pad outline dimensions are typical-for-this-connector-family placeholders,\nNOT measured from Jushuo's real mechanical drawing: that PDF's dimension-drawing page\ndid not yield extractable numeric text with the tooling available in this agent\nenvironment (no pdftotext/poppler-utils, no KiCad GUI to open the part directly).\nThis is an explicit, unresolved verification gap -- flag for a human KiCad-GUI pass\nbefore PCB fab, same caveat class this project already applies to the RP2350 QFN-80\nand PSRAM USON-8 hand-authored footprints." (at 20 360 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid d3d3d5c7-bb11-4ca6-94fd-526311d57df6)
  )
  (text "GPIO assignment: GPIO29 (SPI1 CSn), GPIO30 (SPI1 SCK/RS), GPIO31 (SPI1 TX/MOSI/SDA),\nGPIO32 (D-C/WR), GPIO33 (RESET), GPIO34 (backlight CTRL/enable) -- picked from the generic bidirectional\nGPIO pool rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch exposes as global labels for every RP2350B GPIO not\nalready committed elsewhere. Confirmed free by grepping all of hardware/*.kicad_sch for\nevery GPIOx global label before picking (2026-11-15): input.kicad_sch claims only\nGPIO22-28 (A/B/X/Y + the volume encoder's 3 signals, per the two 2026-11-15 rotary-\nencoder ADRs); esp32_bt.kicad_sch uses named ESP32_* global labels, not GPIOx, and its\nRP2350-side GPIO mapping is still an open item on rp2350b_memory.kicad_sch (not this\nsheet's concern); usb_c.kicad_sch is still an empty skeleton. GPIO29-34 were untouched\nby all of the above. Each GPIOx label keeps the generic pool name as its real net\nidentity (required for it to actually join the same-named label on\nrp2350b_memory.kicad_sch) with a plain, non-connected text caption underneath for the\nlogical function name -- same convention input.kicad_sch uses for A/B/X/Y/VOL_*, and\nfor the same reason: a second schematic label on the same net would trip ERC's\nmultiple_net_names check." (at 20 425 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid b8f19b3b-6bc9-4ba1-b5e8-7c0742da8ef3)
  )
  (text "Backlight driver: the panel's LED_A/LED_K backlight string needs ~9V (VF 8.1-9.9V typ\n9.0V) at 40mA per the datasheet's section 11.1 -- not achievable from the 3.3V/5V rails\ndirectly. U501/L501/C501/C502/R501 are copied directly from Crystalfontz's own 'LED\nBacklight Reference Schematic' (datasheet section 11.2): Diodes AP3036BKTR-G1 (SOT-23-6\nboost LED driver; pin1=CTRL, pin2=VOUT, pin3=VIN, pin4=SW, pin5=GND, pin6=FB per Diodes'\nown AP3036B datasheet DS37004 Rev 2-2), L501 22uH 1210 (VIN-SW), C501 10uF 0805 (VIN\nbypass), C502 1uF 0805 (VOUT-GND), R501 5.1R 0402 (FB-GND, sets ILED = VFB/RFB =\n200mV/5.1R ~= 39.2mA, matching the panel's 40mA spec). VIN comes from this project's\n+3V3 rail (within AP3036B's 2.5-16V input range). CTRL goes to GPIO34 -- tied high\nenables the driver; firmware may instead PWM this same pin for brightness dimming per\nAP3036B's 'High Frequency Dimming Control' feature. Both are valid with this circuit;\nwhich one firmware uses is out of scope for this schematic.\n\nAP3036BKTR-G1 is LCSC C526368 -- re-checked live via the jlcpcb-search MCP tool on\n2026-11-15 (get_component_details, lcsc=C526368): still 0 units in stock, same as this\nbead's own investigation comment found. The bead-named fallback, AW9364DNR (LCSC\nC401007, 11,060 units in stock), was independently checked against its own datasheet\n(downloaded and text-extracted directly, since no pdftotext/poppler was available) --\nit is Awinic's '4-Channel 1-wire Dimming LED Driver', a linear constant-current LED\n*sink* (VIN 2.8V-5.5V, up to 4 LEDs, 20mA/channel sink current, no inductor, no boost\nstage), not a boost converter. It cannot produce this backlight's required ~9V output\nfrom a 3.3V input at all -- this is an architecture mismatch, not just a pinout\ndifference, so it was rejected as a substitute rather than wired in. A further search\nof JLCPCB's 'LED Drivers' category for other in-stock single-cell boost LED drivers\n(PT4115: buck-only, needs 6-30V input; AL1692: AC-DC mains flyback, 8.5-20V input;\nNSI450xx: passive 2-terminal CCRs) found none sharing AP3036B's topology at this input\nvoltage. AP3036BKTR-G1 is kept here as the only verified-correct circuit for this\nbacklight; its 0-stock status is flagged as a sourcing risk for pilink-7el.8 (BOM\ncompilation) to resolve -- wait for restock, find a true topology-equivalent part via\nfurther research, or a human sourcing call -- not a defect in this schematic." (at 20 475 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)))
    (uuid d580fa24-c63c-44b2-a59d-ee9cf513e297)
  )
)
